1. Free use

You may use Sextant at no charge, including in work you are paid to do,
when either of these is true:

a. You build it from this source yourself, and that build is run by you
   or inside the organization that built it.

b. You install a build that Marcus Grenängen publishes on GitHub at
   https://github.com/SneWs/Sextant, including a Windows or macOS file
   on the releases page. An installer or package that only downloads
   that file from GitHub is the same kind of install.

You may be paid for your time to help someone build Sextant from source
for their own use. The build that results stays with that person or
organization under section 1.a.

2. Paid binaries

Marcus Grenängen sells official pre-built binaries for Windows and macOS.
A purchase gives the buyer the right to use that copy. Terms supplied
with the sale apply to that copy together with this license. Where the
sale terms and this license disagree about the purchased copy, the sale
terms control.

3. Source

You may read, copy, and modify the source. You may share the source,
including your modifications, when this license and the copyright notice
stay with the copy.

A person who receives only the source uses it under section 1. Sharing
the source does not include a right to hand on a compiled build.

4. Limits

The permissions above do not allow you to sell Sextant or to charge for
a copy of it. They do not allow you to distribute a compiled build, an
installer, an app bundle, or a package that contains one, except by the
GitHub install in section 1.b.

They do not allow you to present your build as an official Sextant
download. The name Sextant and the Sextant logo identify the official
app. They are not licensed for another product.

5. Contributions

When you submit a change to this repository, you license that change
under this license. You also give Marcus Grenängen a permanent,
royalty-free right to use, modify, and distribute that change, including
in binaries he sells and in builds he publishes on GitHub.

6. No warranty

The source and the GitHub builds are provided as is, without warranty of
any kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. You bear the
risk of using them.

The copyright holder is not liable for any claim, damages, or other
liability arising from this license or from the use of Sextant, whether
in contract, tort, or otherwise.

7. Rights that remain

Rights that this license does not grant stay with the copyright holder.
If you do not agree to this license, do not use, copy, modify, or
